description: Frontend rules (React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn). Senior-level guide.
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css},index.html,vite.config.ts,vercel.json
alwaysApply: false
---

# STACK (fixed, do not add libraries without asking)
React 18, Vite, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui,
TanStack Query, react-router, react-hook-form + zod.
No Redux, no axios, no moment, no UI kit besides shadcn.

# FOLDER STRUCTURE
src/
  pages/            route-level screens (thin: compose hooks + components)
  components/
    ui/             shadcn primitives (do not edit casually)
    <feature>/      bill/, products/, udhaar/, stock/, receipt/, layout/
  hooks/            useProducts, useBills, useCustomers... (TanStack Query)
  lib/
    api/            client.ts + one file per resource (products.ts, bills.ts)
    billing.ts      PURE bill math (subtotal, discount, total, change)
    format.ts       money, quantity, date formatters
    constants.ts
  i18n/             ur.ts, en.ts, index.ts, LanguageContext
  types/            zod schemas + inferred TS types
  styles/           globals.css, print.css

# LAYERS (one pattern per concern)
UI component -> hook -> lib/api -> backend.
- Pages and components NEVER call fetch. Only lib/api does.
- Server data lives in TanStack Query. Do not copy it into useState.
- UI-only state: useState/useReducer. Shared UI state: React context.
- Query keys come from one factory (e.g. queryKeys.products.list(params)).
- After a mutation, invalidate the exact keys it affects.
- Do not use optimistic updates for anything involving money or stock.

# TYPESCRIPT
- strict mode. No `any`, no `as` casts to silence errors, no `// @ts-ignore`.
- Define zod schemas in types/, derive types with z.infer. Validate API
  responses at the boundary (lib/api) so bad data fails loudly there.
- Money and quantity helpers live in lib/format.ts and lib/billing.ts only.
  Round money with Math.round. Never use floats for rupees in storage.
- Bill math must be pure functions with unit tests (Vitest).

# COMPONENTS
- Function components, named exports, props typed with an interface.
- One component per file. Extract when a file passes ~150 lines.
- No business logic inside JSX. Move it to lib/ or a hook.
- Memoize only when you measured a problem (lists of 100+ products are ok).
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML. Always encodeURIComponent for wa.me text.

# FORMS
- react-hook-form + zod for every form. Show errors in the current language.
- Number inputs: type="text" with inputMode="decimal", allow typing "3." and
  "3.5" without the field fighting the user. Parse on blur/submit.
- Autofocus the main field of each screen (search box on New Bill).
- Enter key must work: Enter in search adds the first match.

# I18N AND RTL (non-negotiable)
- ZERO hardcoded user-facing strings in components. Use t("key").
- ur.ts and en.ts have identical keys. Missing English falls back to Urdu.
- Key naming: area.element.purpose (e.g. bill.total.label).
- <html dir lang> updates on language change.
- Use ONLY logical Tailwind classes: ms/me/ps/pe/start/end/text-start/
  text-end/border-s/border-e/rounded-s/rounded-e.
  NEVER ml/mr/pl/pr/left/right/text-left/text-right.
- Directional icons (arrows, chevrons) must flip in RTL (rtl:rotate-180).
- Fonts: Noto Nastaliq Urdu for headings only (give it generous line-height
  so it is not clipped), Noto Sans Arabic for body and numbers, Inter for
  English. Use font-display: swap and real fallback stacks.
- Format numbers with Intl using numberingSystem "latn". Currency: "Rs 1,250".
- Test every screen in both languages before saying it is done.

# UX FOR LOW-TECH SHOPKEEPERS
- Primary action buttons min-height 56px, secondary min 44px, thumb reachable
  on phones. Big readable text (base 18px, totals 32px+).
- One tap for common actions. Avoid modals; prefer inline panels. For
  destructive actions (delete a bill line) act immediately and show an
  "Undo" toast instead of a confirm dialog.
- Never rely on color alone: pair color with text or icon.
- Colors: green = confirm, red = delete/udhaar/danger, blue = normal.
- Every screen needs: loading state (skeleton), empty state (helpful text),
  and error state (bilingual message + retry).
- Totals use aria-live="polite". Visible focus rings. Labels on all inputs.
- Do not hide the shop's most common path (New Bill) behind menus.

# BILL DRAFT SAFETY
- The bill being built is held in a useReducer + context and persisted to
  localStorage on every change, so refresh or phone sleep never loses it.
- Create the bill UUID (crypto.randomUUID) when the bill starts. Reuse it on
  retry. Disable "Make Bill" while saving.
- On any save error, KEEP the bill on screen and show a clear message.
  Clear the draft only after the server confirms.

# API CLIENT (lib/api/client.ts)
- Base URL from import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL. Attach JWT. Throw a typed
  ApiError (status, code, message).
- If a request takes > 3s, surface a "server is waking up" message (free
  hosting sleeps) and allow retry. Handle offline with a bilingual message.
- 401 -> clear token and go to login. Never log tokens or passwords.

# PERFORMANCE (cheap Android phones)
- Lazy-load routes. Initial JS target < 250 KB gzipped.
- Debounce search ~150ms. Filter the cached product list on the client.
- Images: lazy-load, set width/height, serve WebP (<150 KB, max 800px,
  resized in the browser before upload).
- No heavy libraries for small jobs (no chart lib: use plain divs).

# PRINTING (receipt)
- Browser window.print only. print.css hides everything except <Receipt/>.
- @page size 80mm auto (or 58mm per shop setting), margin 0, black on white,
  no images/colors/shadows. Urdu receipt uses Noto Sans Arabic, RTL.
- Preview the receipt on screen at the real width.

# SECURITY (frontend)
- Never put secrets in the frontend. Only VITE_API_URL is allowed.
- Hide owner-only UI for cashiers, but remember the backend is the real guard.
- Validate and trim user input; never trust data from localStorage blindly
  (parse with zod, fall back to defaults).

# TESTING
- Vitest for lib/billing.ts and lib/format.ts (discount %, decimals,
  rounding, udhaar balance display). Keep tests small and fast.
- Do not write brittle snapshot tests.

# DEFINITION OF DONE (run before saying "done")
1. `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` pass with no errors or warnings.
2. Lint passes. No unused imports or variables.
3. Checked at 360px phone width and desktop, in Urdu AND English.
4. No hardcoded strings, no left/right Tailwind classes.
5. Loading, empty, and error states exist.
6. List the files changed and how I can test it in 3 steps.
